# Collectors and transports

Device collection is **READ-ONLY**. Positive allowlist is mandatory.

Never accept an arbitrary command from API, MCP, request body, tenant config, database, or a remote user. Transport is not “SSH as a service”.

Protocol fallback (SSH vs Telnet vs API) must be **configured and tested**. Do not add opportunistic fallback onto destructive or unproven commands.

CODE PASS ≠ LIVE PASS. Lab validation is optional, private, and never writes real output into Git fixtures.

## MikroTik

- Support **many routers per tenant**. Never assume “this tenant’s DHCP is on MikroTik X”.
- The same MAC on multiple devices is information, not automatically an error.
- Allow only explicitly supported **read** operations (print/get style). No `add` / `set` / `remove` / `enable` / `disable` / `move`.
- Parser failure must not trigger a mutable fallback command.

## Intelbras G08 (OLT)

OLT is an independent source. Driver/family/version defines supported behavior — do not “try commands until one works”.

Proven MAC-table command for this family:

`show ont mac-address-table interface gpon all`

Do not confuse **ONT-ID**, **serial (SN)**, **GEM**, **PON/interface**, **VID**. Multiple MACs behind one ONU are normal.

## Completeness

Every run must classify honestly: **complete | partial | failed | indeterminate**.

If the command ran but the parser dropped lines, it is **not** complete. Record seen/created/updated, parse failures, sanitized errors, timestamps, collector version, device/source.

Current `collection_runs` also stores `status` plus `completeness` (`complete` / `partial` / `none` / `unknown`). Keep the classification honest; renaming enums is a versioned contract, not a silent change.

